{artist: Terry Gilkyson}
{year: 1964}
{key: F}
{define: "First note" copy "c"}
{meta: firstline Look for the bare necessities}
{meta: movie The Jungle Book}

[<hidden>First note</hidden>]

{start_of_chorus}
Look for the [F] bare necessities, the [Bb]simple bare ne[Bb7]cessities
For[F]get about your [D7]worries and your [G7]strife.
[C7] I mean the [F] bare ne[F7]cessities, or [Bb]Mother Nature's [Bb7]recipes
That [F]bring the [D7]bare ne[G7]cessi[C7]ties of [F]life  [Bb7] [F]
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Verse}
Wherever I [C7]wander, wherever I [F]roam
I couldn't be [C7]fonder of my big [F]home
[F] The bees are [Bb]buzzin' in the [Bbm]tree
To make some [F]honey just for [G7]me
[D7]You look under the [D7]rocks and plants
And [Gm]take a glance at the [G7]fancy [C7]ants, then [F]maybe try a [D7]few

The bare ne[Gm]cessities of [C7]life will come to [F]you [D7]
[G7] They'll [C7]come to [F]you! [Eb7] [F]

{start_of_chorus}
Look for the [F] bare necessities, the [Bb]simple bare ne[Bb7]cessities
For[F]get about your [D7]worries and your [G7]strife.
[C7] I mean the [F] bare ne[F7]cessities, that's [Bb]why a bear can [Bb7]rest at ease
With [F]just the [D7]bare ne[G7]cessi[C7]ties of [F]life  [Bb7] [F]
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Verse}
When you pick a [C7]paw-paw or a prickly [F7]pear
And you prick a [C7]raw paw, well, next time be[F]ware
[F7] Don't pick the [Bb]prickly pear by the [Bbm]paw
When you pick a [F]pear try to use the [G7]claw
But [D7]you don't need to [D7]use the claw
When you [Gm]pick a pear of the [Gm]big paw-[C7]paw
Have I [F]given you a [D7]clue?

The bare ne[Gm]cessities of [C7]life will come to [F]you [D7]
[G7] They'll [C7]come to [F]you! [Eb7] [F]

